= ME/CFS-Specific Research Methods
<ch:research-methods-mecfs>

#chapter-abstract[
Why ME/CFS research is methodologically hard: case definition heterogeneity, lack of objective endpoints, PEM as a constraint on study participation (selection bias), the 2-day CPET reliability debate, subjective outcomes in unblinded trials, appropriate control group selection, biomarker overfitting in small samples, statistical power with heterogeneous populations, and the problem of replicating findings across diagnostic criteria.

